  "final_answer_preview": "According to Section 309(6) of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, if a person causes hurt while committing or attempting to commit robbery, they may face imprisonment for life or rigorous imprisonment for a term that may extend to ten years, along with a fine. Additionally, Section 309(5) states that anyone who attempts to commit robbery can be punished with rigorous imprisonment for up to seven years and a fine. Furthermore, Section 313 specifies that individuals belonging to a gang habitually committing robbery may also face rigorous imprisonment for up to seven years and a fine.",
